some is gone, when is my pool refreshed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","user":"Colognian","date":". 09-23-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:04:52-07:00","id":975259,"title":"","content":"I'm using M20 version","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:27:18-07:00","id":975267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975209-extra-quintessence?p=975258#post975258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understood this part of the rules.<br /> <br /> E. g. if I have avatar 3, then I spend 3 quintessenz.<br /> <br /> How much is left on my track?<br /> <br /> Three or Zero?<br /> <br /> If some is gone, when is my pool refreshed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only way to get Quintessence without Prime is either by meditating at a node or drawing it up from a periapt.<br /> When you draw it up from a node, RAW you can only have as much as your Avatar rating allows. Having Prime 1 removes this limit, allowing you up to 20 points Paradox permitting.<br /> <br /> If you have Avatar 3, you can use up to 3 points at any one time. This means you can use fewer if you want. Without Prime the only thing you can really use Quint on is lowering Magical Difficulty and healing Agg damage (Life 4), so you don't really need all that much Quint. Plus, I think the Avatar limit only really applies to Quint used for lowering Arete roll difficulty and drawing from nodes via meditation.<br /> <br /> Prime users, however, have almost all their effects involve Quintessence, either by enchanting, making wonders, moving the stuff about, or just throwing at people as bolts of pain, it all requires Quintessence to pull off, so naturally they're going to need a heck of a lot more than other mages.<br /> <br /> Prime users are still limited by their Avatar rating for drawing Quint out of a node the old fashioned way, so if they have Avatar 3, they can only do 3 Quint worth of stuff within a single effect like shooting bolts of prime or enchanting swords, etc. Yes, this means that being a Prime mage with Avatar 1 sucks, though there are optional rules allowing Prime mages to use their Prime sphere worth of Quint instead.<br /> <br /> That being said, Prime mages can use Prime 2 to draw Quint out of a node, Periapt, Tass, Juncture, Talisman, Person (ouch), and forgo the Avatar limit. Also creating Wonders goes around the Avatar limit too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"